Q: Found DB delays in application - how will you improve that provide steps.
    Database bottlenecks are a common cause of high API latency in Spring Boot microservices.
    1. Identify Slow Queries
        Find out database slow query logs (e.g., PostgreSQL slow_log, MySQL slow query log) to pinpoint statements
        taking longer than an acceptable threshold (e.g., >200ms).
    2. Analyze Execution Plans
        Check:
            execution plan
            full table scans
            unnecessary joins
            missing indexes
            inefficient WHERE conditions
            sorting large datasets
            unnecessary columns
            N+1 queries
    3. Check and resolve N+1 Query Problems
        Inspect Hibernate/JPA logs for excessive query generation.
        Fix N+1 issues by using @EntityGraph, JOIN FETCH, or batch fetching (@BatchSize) in your Spring Data JPA repositories.
        Verify success by observing a dramatic reduction in total executed SQL queries per API request in the logs.
    4. Implement Caching
        Introduce distributed caching (e.g., Redis) using Spring's @Cacheable annotation for read-heavy, low-volatility reference data.
        Verify success by checking cache hit ratios and noting a drop in database CPU utilization.
    5. Tune Connection Pooling
        Tune HikariCP settings in application.yml (e.g., maximum-pool-size, connection-timeout, idle-timeout) to match your database
        server's capacity and concurrency requirements.
        Verify success by eliminating connection acquisition timeouts under peak load tests.
    6. Check database health
        Investigate:
            CPU
            memory
            I/O
            locks
            deadlocks
            long-running transactions
            connection count
            replication lag
            storage performance
    7. Pagination
       Avoid loading huge datasets:
           Page<Order> findByCustomerId(
               Long customerId,
               Pageable pageable
           );
       Instead of:
        SELECT millions of rows
